@*
    The mark of an outside tool: GitHub, GitHub Copilot, Claude, VS Code.

    Every component in this family needs one, so the rules that keep them
    legible are enforced in one file rather than remembered in ten.

    Drawn here rather than fetched. A component that needs the network to show
    itself is no use in a WebView with no egress — the same argument CopyButton
    and OpenFolderButton already make about their own glyphs — so each mark is a
    path in this file and there is no CDN, no icon font and no second asset to
    ship.

    Filled, never stroked, and that is the family's legibility rule: provider
    marks are filled and state icons are stroked at 1.6. A filled shape and a
    1.6-weight outline read as different classes of thing even at 16 px and even
    when both inherit the same ink, so a reader never mistakes a provider for a
    state. Everything is currentColor, so the same GitHub path is the live ink on
    an open issue chip and the disabled ink on a Connect button, with no variant.

    These are the providers' own published monochrome marks. The alternative — a
    per-provider abstract glyph, GitHub a circle with a dot, Copilot a rounded
    visor, Claude a radial burst, VS Code a pair of angle brackets — is drawn up
    and ready if the marks ever have to go, and it is worth being clear about
    what it costs. At Compact density the mark is the only thing separating a
    Claude session row from a Copilot session row from a GitHub issue row: the
    label is gone, the state chip says "Running" for both, and three abstract
    circles would make that density unreadable rather than merely generic.

    The viewBox is 24x24 rather than the 16x16 the state icons use, because that
    is the coordinate system all four marks are published in and re-plotting a
    trademark by hand is how a mark stops being the mark. Nothing downstream
    sees it: width and height come from Size either way.
*@

@if (Provider is not IntegrationProvider.None)
{
    <svg class="@ClassValue"
         viewBox="0 0 24 24"
         width="@Size"
         height="@Size"
         fill="currentColor"
         role="@(Labelled ? "img" : null)"
         aria-hidden="@(Labelled ? null : "true")"
         focusable="false"
         data-testid="@TestId">
        @if (Labelled)
        {
            <title>@Title</title>
        }
        <path d="@Path" />
    </svg>
}

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IntegrationProvider Provider { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Edge length in pixels. Sized from the row rather than from the
    /// font, because a mark that grew with the type would stop matching the
    /// state icon beside it at exactly the moment a reader zoomed in.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public int Size { get; set; } = 16;

    /// <summary>Names the mark to assistive technology, and only then. A mark
    /// beside its own text label would otherwise be announced twice, so the
    /// default is hidden — and Compact density, where the mark is the sole
    /// differentiator, is the case that passes one.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Title { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; }

    private bool Labelled => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Title);

    private string ClassValue
    {
        get
        {
            var mark = $"provider-mark provider-mark--{IntegrationStates.SlugOf(Provider)}";
            return string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? mark : $"{mark} {CssClass}";
        }
    }

    private string Path => Provider switch
    {
        IntegrationProvider.GitHub => GitHub,
        IntegrationProvider.Copilot => Copilot,
        IntegrationProvider.Claude => Claude,
        IntegrationProvider.VsCode => VsCode,
        _ => string.Empty
    };

